==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|straungely|t=strangely, aloofly, intricately}}; equivalent to {{af|en|strange|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɹeɪnd͡ʒli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-strangely.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[strange]] or [[coincidental]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|Though I'd never gone to Boston before, everything looked '''strangely''' familiar.}}
#: {{ux|en|Daniel was walking '''strangely''' because he had twisted his ankle.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1996|title=Film Review
|passage=A tale of gangland warfare and filial loyalty in the Glasgow of 1958, ''Small Faces'' is an enjoyable but '''strangely''' unmoving film.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Surprisingly, wonderfully.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest||4|1|text={{...}}all thy vexations / Were but my trials of thy love, and thou / Hast '''strangely''' stood the test{{...}}}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|oddly}}
* {{l|en|uncannily}}
* {{l|en|weirdly}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|strangely warmed}}

